            "To solve this problem, we need to find the remainder when $N$ is divided by $1000$.\n\n1. **Understanding the Problem**:\n   - We have 16 chairs arranged in a row.\n   - Each person selects a chair, and no person sits next to two other people.\n\n2. **Counting the Possible Subsets**:\n   - There are $16!$ ways to choose the 16 chairs.\n   - Since each person selects a chair, there are $16!$ ways to choose the 16 chairs for each person.\n\n3. **Calculating the Number of Subsets**:\n   - The number of subsets of 16 chairs is $16! / (16! \\times 16!)$.\n   - This simplifies to $16! / (16! \\times 16! \\times 16!)$.\n\n4. **Finding the Remainder**:\n   - The remainder when $N$ is divided by $1000$ is the number of subsets of 16 chairs that are divisible by $1000$.\n   - The number of subsets of 16 chairs that are divisible by $1000$ is $16! / (16! \\times 16! \\times 16!)$.\n   - This simplifies to $16! / (16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16!)$.\n\n5. **Calculating the Remainder**:\n   - The remainder when $N$ is divided by $1000$ is $16! / (16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16!)$.\n   - This simplifies to $16! / (16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16!)$.\n\n6. **Conclusion**:\n   - The remainder when $N$ is divided by $1000$ is $16! / (16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16!)$.\n   - This simplifies to $16! / (16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16!)$.\n\nTherefore, the remainder when $N$ is divided by $1000$ is $\\boxed{16! / (16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! \\times 16! 